Almost a year ago, there was a thread in this forum about making the 
Sokoban maps random.  I really thought this was a great idea (thanks, 
Klaus Kassner).  So I have been working on it for some time, even though 
I haven't actually played NetHack since 3.4.2.

Below are some results of my program.  It's far from finished, but now 
I'm starting to get some decent results I dare to show in public :)

Some notes though:
* I took the liberty to display boulders as a (#) for clarity.
* In each map there is only one pit/hole (^).  This is for efficiency. 
You should think that there is a whole row of those like in "real" 
Sokoban maps.
* Every boulder should be potted, there are no spare boulders.

I'd really like some feedback on this, so go ahead.  If you want to play 
them, use the following link.  It contains all the sources, also a very 
minimal playing program (at the moment I haven't integrated anything 
into NetHack yet):
http://cage.ugent.be/~jdemeyer/nethack/sokogen.tgz

This does the trick to play: (should work on most GNU/Linux systems, I 
have to figure out autoconf some time)

make && ./play retry-success/*

Note that the tarball also has the sources for the generator, but I 
would not really recommend reading it.  The code is not all that well 
documented and is likely to change significantly in the future.  If I 
get positive replies, I will probably put up a page explaining the 
algorithm detail.

